tesla,2026-03,438000,1717000,1665490,1974550,372300,547500,1.0,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart: monthly values vector-extracted from the Q4-2025 and Q1-2026 update-deck PDFs (overlapping months agree within ~3k mi; 658k end-2025, 1.717M end-Mar-2026). Texas driverless service only — the Q3-2025 call tracks Bay Area as a separate supervised series (1M+ mi by Oct 2025) and Aug-2025's ~13k delta is too small to contain the Bay fleet. Read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test); if 'paid' is literally passenger-on-board miles the true total is higher, so kyoom_max carries ~15% upside and kyoom_min ~3% read noise."
waymo,2026-03,17700000,220450000,219850000,221050000,13275000,22125000,1.0,1,1,1,"US est.: calibrated to Waymo's 220.6M rider-only miles through Mar 2026 (Jun 24, 2026 update); per-city cumulative PHX 80.6M, SF 67.1M, LA 51.8M, ATX 15.8M, ATL 5.4M; CPUC Q1-2026 CA driverless actuals 9.09M Jan/8.19M Feb/9.11M Mar (52.9% CA share) corroborate level and shape within ~4%; ±25%"
tesla,2026-04,374000,2091000,2028270,2404650,317900,467500,1.0,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart: monthly values vector-extracted from the Q2-2026 update-deck PDF (13 points through Jun-2026, 2.440M end-Q2; overlapping months re-confirm the earlier decks' series within ~8k mi). Austin + Dallas/Houston (unsupervised D/H launch Apr 18, 2026); Bay Area remains a separate supervised series. Read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test); if 'paid' is literally passenger-on-board miles the true total is higher, so kyoom_max carries ~15% upside and kyoom_min ~3% read noise. (Pre-pin activity-ratio estimates ran ~28% high for Q2 — utilization-led slowdown the fleet counts missed.)"
waymo,2026-04,19000000,239450000,235989717,242910283,16139717,21860283,1.0,1,1,1,"US est.: extrapolated from the 220.6M end-Mar-2026 anchor (Jun 24, 2026 update) at >4M rider-only mi/week with modest growth (~3,600-3,750 cars); ±30% CPUC Q2-2026 (posted Aug 18, 2026) CA driverless actuals: 9,414,525 deployment + 51,198 pilot = 9,465,724 mi this month (TotalVMTZEV, all three periods incl. deadhead), so ~50% of the estimate is now regulator-measured rather than modeled; the +/-30% modeling band is applied to the non-California remainder only."
